WEBVTT

NOTE Machine draft — owner proofreading required before production.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
Here's a good example of an install

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.080
that we're wrapping up today.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.160
You can see that we selected specific plants

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.640
for specific locations.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.360
And why that's so important is in five years from now,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.240
we don't want you to drive by your home and go,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.980
why are those bushes covering my windows

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.900
when we are trying to avoid that?

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.960
So we make specific selections to avoid doing that.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.800
Basically you have like,

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.720
for example, green velvet boxwoods.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.640
These will grow into about 30 to 36 inches at max.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.000
And they're very easy to trim and maintain at that space.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.160
This particular crate Myrtle is a Muscogee.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.960
And this one will fill in this space

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.100
above these two windows really well,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.220
as well as provide a big plethora of color in the summer.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.380
This is a very good full sun, full heat area.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.000
So this plant will thrive in this area.
